// @test regression/INV156-tail-qualifier-fold
// @description A user function whose body TAIL is a statement-form `if` returns the join of the CONDITION and both branch values, so a series condition makes the call `series` even when both branches are const. `plot`'s `title` is const-only, so cell (1) is TV's CE10123 and cell (2) - the identical shape under a const condition - must stay clean, which is what pins the qualifier to the condition rather than to a blanket promotion. Cells (3) and (4) already worked before the fix and guard the switch and ternary tails against regressing. All four adjudicated against `pine-lint --tv` 2026-08-25. See INV156, TODO #68.
// @expects parse: success
// @expects errors: 3
// @expects error: line=10, message=/"series string".*"const string"/
// @expects error: line=25, message=/"series string".*"const string"/
// @expects error: line=30, message=/"series string".*"const string"/
//@version=6
indicator("tail qualifier fold")

// (1) statement-form `if` tail under a SERIES condition -> series string
seriesTail() =>
    if close > open
        "a"
    else
        "b"
plot(close, title = seriesTail())

// (2) the identical shape under a CONST condition -> stays const, clean
constTail() =>
    if 1 > 0
        "a"
    else
        "b"
plot(close, title = constTail())

// (3) switch tail - correct before the fix, guard against regressing
switchTail() =>
    switch
        close > open => "a"
        => "b"
plot(close, title = switchTail())

// (4) ternary tail - correct before the fix, guard against regressing
ternaryTail() =>
    close > open ? "a" : "b"
plot(close, title = ternaryTail())
